Per-container context file. Copy to `<container-path>/AGENTS.md` (or CLAUDE.md
if your harness prefers that name) and fill in.

WHY this file and not the wiki: nested context files are read by proximity —
only when an agent touches this folder. A root CLAUDE.md is injected into every
sub-agent, so anything container-specific placed there is multiplied by the
whole run's agent count and paid mostly by agents working somewhere else. This
is the same cost logic as `rules.md` being global-only.

Keep it under one screen. If it grows past that, the container is doing too much.
Everything here should be true of THIS container specifically — anything true of
the whole project belongs in `.wiki/`, and anything mechanically checkable
belongs in `containers.yaml` instead of prose.
-->

